&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;At Klaviyo, we value the unique backgrounds, experiences and perspectives each Klaviyo (we call ourselves Klaviyos) brings to our workplace each and every day. We believe everyone deserves a fair shot at success and appreciate the experiences each person brings beyond the traditional job requirements. If you’re a close but not exact match with the description, we hope you’ll still consider applying. Want to learn more about life at Klaviyo? Visit &lt;a class=&quot;_ymio1r31 _ypr0glyw _zcxs1o36 _mizu194a _1ah3dkaa _ra3xnqa1 _128mdkaa _1cvmnqa1 _4davt94y _4bfu18uv _1hms8stv _ajmmnqa1 _vchhusvi _kqswh2mm _ect4ttxp _syaz13af _1a3b18uv _4fpr8stv _5goinqa1 _f8pj13af _9oik18uv _1bnxglyw _jf4cnqa1 _30l313af _1nrm18uv _c2waglyw _1iohnqa1 _9h8h12zz _10531ra0 _1ien1ra0 _n0fx1ra0 _1vhv17z1&quot; href=&quot;http://klaviyo.com/careers&quot; data-renderer-mark=&quot;true&quot;&gt;klaviyo.com/careers&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;to see how we empower creators to own their own destiny.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Klaviyo&#39;s Champions program is one of the most visible and strategically significant customer programs in the company. It brings together a curated group of Klaviyo&#39;s most engaged, influential customers — deepening their relationship with the brand, amplifying their voices externally, and embedding them into the teams that build and market the product.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The goal isn&#39;t just a well-run program. It&#39;s a recognized one. Think Salesforce Trailblazers — a program with genuine industry clout, where being a Klaviyo Champion means something beyond the company walls. The infrastructure and early foundation are in place. What this role requires now is someone who can elevate the program&#39;s prestige, deepen internal activation, and prove its impact in business terms.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a high-ownership, high-visibility IC role with significant cross-functional scope. This person will regularly represent the Champions program to senior stakeholders across the business.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Program operations &amp;amp; member experience: &lt;/strong&gt;Own the day-to-day operations of the Champions program including strategic planning, recruitment and onboarding, member communications, virtual and in-person experiences, and overall member engagement. Maintain program health and quality as it scales, ensuring every member feels the weight and value of what it means to be a Klaviyo Champion.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Internal enablement &amp;amp; activation: &lt;/strong&gt;Support Champions&#39; presence across the product development and go-to-market lifecycle by leading cross-functional projects with Marketing, PMM, Product, R&amp;amp;D, CS, and Partnerships to surface Champion voices at key moments — product research, beta testing, case studies, reference calls, events, content, and social media. Help shift activation from being concentrated at launch to a more consistent presence earlier in the lifecycle.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ROI &amp;amp; measurement: &lt;/strong&gt;Contribute to the continued development of the program&#39;s measurement framework, following established methods and processes, to help demonstrate the business value of the Champions program in concrete terms.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Program prestige &amp;amp; industry recognition: &lt;/strong&gt;Support the Champions program&#39;s external reputation and visibility by helping members build their professional profile and ensuring the program reflects well on their relationship with Klaviyo.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Budget management:&lt;/strong&gt; Support administration of the Champions program budget and help inform spend decisions that reflect program priorities and member experience goals.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHAT SUCCESS LOOKS LIKE&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Champions is embedded across the full product and GTM lifecycle — from early research through launch — not concentrated at any single stage&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The program has measurable industry recognition; members cite it as a meaningful professional credential, and peers in the market know what it stands for&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Members feel genuinely recognized and engaged, with clear evidence of value from their perspective&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A reliable ROI framework is in place and being reported on regularly&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;References, case studies, product feedback, and thought leadership pipelines are consistently active and well-utilized across the business&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The program grows in quality and clout without losing the relationship-driven character that makes it work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHAT YOU BRING&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years in customer advocacy, community, customer marketing, or a closely related function — B2B SaaS experience strongly preferred&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience running or contributing significantly to a structured advocacy or champions-style program, within established processes and operational policies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience thinking about program prestige alongside program operations — brand, positioning, and member value, not just logistics&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong cross-functional instincts — comfortable leading a cross-functional project and advising peers across Marketing, Product, R&amp;amp;D, and CS&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analytical enough to contribute to a measurement framework — you understand what program ROI looks like and have helped build or evolve one before&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong program management skills — this program is highly visible and operationally complex; rigor without rigidity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written and verbal communication; you can tell a compelling story about customer impact to internal stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable supporting budget administration and spend decisions within established guidelines&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Candidates with transferable experience in program management, customer success, or partnerships will be considered — advocacy and community experience is ideal but not the only path in&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Massachusetts Applicants:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;It is unlawful in Massachusetts to require or administer a lie detector test as a condition of employment or continued employment. An employer who violates this law shall be subject to criminal penalties and civil liability.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our salary range reflects the cost of labor across various U.S. geographic markets. The range displayed below reflects the minimum and maximum target salaries for the position across all our US locations. The base salary offered for this position is determined by several factors, including the applicant’s job-related skills, relevant experience, education or training, and work location.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In addition to base salary, our total compensation package may include participation in the company’s annual cash bonus plan, variable compensation (OTE) for sales and customer success roles, equity, sign-on payments, and a comprehensive range of health, welfare, and wellbeing benefits based on eligibility.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Your recruiter can provide more details about the specific salary/OTE range for your preferred location during the hiring process.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Base Pay Range For US Locations:&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$88,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$132,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;This role may require up to 10% travel for purposes such as new hire onboarding, client or partner work if applicable, team meetings, and industry events. Travel is coordinated in advance.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Get to Know Klaviyo&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re Klaviyo (pronounced clay-vee-oh). We empower creators to own their destiny by making first-party data accessible and actionable like never before. We see limitless potential for the technology we’re developing to nurture personalized experiences in ecommerce and beyond. To reach our goals, we need our own crew of remarkable creators—ambitious and collaborative teammates who stay focused on our north star: delighting our customers. If you’re ready to do the best work of your career, where you’ll be welcomed as your whole self from day one and supported with generous benefits, we hope you’ll join us.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;AI fluency at Klaviyo includes responsible use of AI (including privacy, security, bias awareness, and human-in-the-loop). We provide accommodations as needed.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
